{
 "about": "Flavor objects (owner, 2026-10-18): single small standalone pieces scattered through each spawn area, each on clean open ground, never composed into scenes (the scenes were dropped as illogical to look at). No piece may share its art with anything a player can own or pick up (check_deco.py; 'allowed' lists the justified hits), only single-tile art from the classic set, nothing that needs a wall, a tree or a companion piece. 'themes' and 'assemblies' are the dropped scene design, kept for reference. Each theme also has a 'color' list (owner, 2026-10-18: 'add some additional items with more color'): wildflowers and red-capped mushrooms, placed on new sites added beside the existing pieces, so a world that has the first pieces gains only the new ones. The flavor objects are written into the map's own statics (owner, 2026-10-18: they must look like the map's decoration, not highlight on hover), so no piece may be impassable or a raised surface: stock house placement refuses a static that is either (HousePlacement.Check), and the owner said they must not block buildable space for houses. check_deco.py refuses such art.",
